1
00:00:14,040 --> 00:00:18,380
Aiming for the sunset
floating over the Nakagawa,

2
00:00:18,380 --> 00:00:23,860
I kicked a pebble and it
flew off through the clouds,

3
00:00:24,440 --> 00:00:29,320
joking around with Kashiwa from gym class,

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,760
they laughed and said I was
still as full of energy as ever.

5
00:00:33,760 --> 00:00:37,400
Even if I somehow stir
up some spirit somewhere,

6
00:00:37,400 --> 00:00:38,640
there's only one way: to win.

7
00:00:38,640 --> 00:00:41,900
A nightmare, and the unchanging streetscape,

8
00:00:41,900 --> 00:00:43,840
are gentler than ever.

9
00:00:44,660 --> 00:00:46,820
Because the crows are cawing,

10
00:00:46,820 --> 00:00:48,680
the sun has already gone down.

11
00:00:49,760 --> 00:00:51,900
Stuffing our mouths with yakitori,

12
00:00:51,900 --> 00:00:53,800
even just looking at it...

13
00:00:54,680 --> 00:00:57,420
of the pointed hat,

14
00:00:57,420 --> 00:01:04,020
the sunset falls from the
waterworks to Ōishi-den.

15
00:01:06,700 --> 00:01:10,020
Tomorrow too,
it'll end in another failure, won't it.

16
00:01:10,020 --> 00:01:13,620
Katsushika, for a while,
happiness was lost too.

17
00:01:13,620 --> 00:01:16,260
Because I'm a fool who finally realized it.

18
00:01:24,840 --> 00:01:27,360
Run! The ringer sports day!

19
00:01:37,400 --> 00:01:40,340
Phew, time for a little break.

20
00:01:45,480 --> 00:01:48,080
Tea after a day's work tastes so good.

21
00:01:51,760 --> 00:01:52,640
Chief.

22
00:01:53,820 --> 00:01:56,180
Hideo, your legs are wobbling!

23
00:01:57,740 --> 00:02:01,580
Hopeless, Hideo.
You're obviously lacking exercise.

24
00:02:02,740 --> 00:02:03,780
Dad, are you okay?

25
00:02:05,060 --> 00:02:05,940
I'm fine.

26
00:02:06,520 --> 00:02:08,400
Next, we do knee bends.

27
00:02:10,560 --> 00:02:12,940
One, two, one, two,

28
00:02:13,460 --> 00:02:14,920
Dad, your body's so stiff.

29
00:02:16,080 --> 00:02:18,180
I'm really trying my best, you know.

30
00:02:19,160 --> 00:02:22,568
Ngh, ow ow

31
00:02:22,618 --> 00:02:25,040
But I made it.

32
00:02:25,300 --> 00:02:27,120
It means if you try, you can do it.

33
00:02:28,040 --> 00:02:28,740
Ryotsu.

34
00:02:28,960 --> 00:02:29,860
Ryo-san.

35
00:02:30,580 --> 00:02:31,060
No.

36
00:02:31,480 --> 00:02:34,940
Not "no." You were loafing around here again,
weren't you?

37
00:02:35,180 --> 00:02:38,800
Well, no, that's not it.
I was on patrol in the park.

38
00:02:40,340 --> 00:02:41,300
Th-that's painful.

39
00:02:41,300 --> 00:02:41,900
Hey, whoa.

40
00:02:41,900 --> 00:02:43,120
Uuuugh.

41
00:02:43,820 --> 00:02:46,660
Anyway, what's going on? Bu-chuun!

42
00:02:47,060 --> 00:02:48,560
Is it because it's autumn,
the season of sports?

43
00:02:49,600 --> 00:02:51,540
Well, actually...

44
00:02:53,320 --> 00:02:55,240
Daisuke's sports day?

45
00:02:55,660 --> 00:02:58,580
At my school,
parents take part along with the students,

46
00:02:58,580 --> 00:03:01,900
split into red and white teams to compete.

47
00:03:02,680 --> 00:03:04,140
We're going to win!

48
00:03:04,440 --> 00:03:05,920
Ryo-san, come watch too.

49
00:03:05,920 --> 00:03:09,360
Well said, Daisuke! That's the spirit!

50
00:03:10,600 --> 00:03:14,220
So the Chief is personally training
his son-in-law and grandson.

51
00:03:14,220 --> 00:03:17,200
What a beautiful family bond.

52
00:03:17,720 --> 00:03:19,480
That made me tear up.

53
00:03:20,040 --> 00:03:22,320
Stop with the contrived sentiment.

54
00:03:22,320 --> 00:03:26,280
You wouldn't understand,
since you only move for money.

55
00:03:26,840 --> 00:03:28,540
You saw right through me.

56
00:03:29,600 --> 00:03:32,400
Alright, next, sprint to that slide.

57
00:03:34,440 --> 00:03:35,760
We'll do five rounds.

58
00:03:36,700 --> 00:03:37,580
Ready...

59
00:03:39,360 --> 00:03:41,500
Alright, Daisuke, go!

60
00:03:41,500 --> 00:03:43,420
Dad, don't lose either!

61
00:03:48,600 --> 00:03:49,480
Goal!

62
00:03:49,480 --> 00:03:51,240
Just a little more, hang in there!

63
00:03:51,240 --> 00:03:52,560
Goal!

64
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:55,400
Right, second set!

65
00:03:56,280 --> 00:04:01,700
Yeah, that's it!

66
00:04:01,700 --> 00:04:03,960
You're getting better and better!

67
00:04:08,580 --> 00:04:09,200
Aaaaaah!

68
00:04:11,380 --> 00:04:36,300
Eeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeee
Good, good, good, good, good, good, good, good, good, good, good, good, good, good

69
00:04:36,300 --> 00:04:38,120
Ryotsu, give me a hand!

70
00:04:38,120 --> 00:04:38,640
Yes!

71
00:04:41,040 --> 00:04:43,780
At this rate, you won't be able to
make it to tomorrow's sports day.

72
00:04:43,780 --> 00:04:46,080
I-I'm fine.

73
00:04:46,080 --> 00:04:47,400
If you rest overnight,

74
00:04:47,400 --> 00:04:50,220
pushing yourself will only slow
your recovery down even more.

75
00:04:50,820 --> 00:04:52,580
Hideo, don't worry.

76
00:04:52,580 --> 00:04:54,300
I'll take care of it.

77
00:04:57,160 --> 00:04:59,200
You want me to take part in your place?

78
00:04:59,480 --> 00:05:01,680
Daisuke is working so hard.

79
00:05:01,680 --> 00:05:03,740
How could I just leave it alone?

80
00:05:03,740 --> 00:05:05,640
Hideo can't take part,

81
00:05:06,300 --> 00:05:09,800
and you're the only one who's strong and free.
It's for Daisuke.

82
00:05:10,100 --> 00:05:10,880
But, well...

83
00:05:11,380 --> 00:05:12,960
Ryo-chan, you should go.

84
00:05:13,460 --> 00:05:17,000
You always hog all the prizes at the sports day,
don't you?

85
00:05:17,840 --> 00:05:21,380
Hold on a second. You can't just
suddenly say something like that.

86
00:05:21,540 --> 00:05:23,580
I have a schedule too, you know.

87
00:05:24,500 --> 00:05:28,760
Sure enough, your Sunday schedule
is packed solid, isn't it?

88
00:05:29,200 --> 00:05:31,555
Up at 2 p.m., pachinko until 5,

89
00:05:31,605 --> 00:05:33,260
then TV until midnight.

90
00:05:33,380 --> 00:05:34,020
Fine, I'll do it.

91
00:05:36,300 --> 00:05:37,600
You just want that, don't you.

92
00:05:38,420 --> 00:05:39,860
Come on, Chief.

93
00:05:39,860 --> 00:05:43,360
That makes me sound like
I'm obsessed with money.

94
00:05:43,820 --> 00:05:44,540
I see.

95
00:05:44,540 --> 00:05:45,240
Well then,

96
00:05:45,780 --> 00:05:46,780
I'm free.

97
00:05:46,780 --> 00:05:49,940
As it happens,
my schedule is wide open all day that day.

98
00:05:49,940 --> 00:05:51,820
Wow, that was fast.

99
00:05:51,820 --> 00:05:54,860
That's the instinct for money at work

100
00:05:54,860 --> 00:05:59,740
No matter what happens, you make sure
Daisuke's red team wins the championship!

101
00:05:59,740 --> 00:06:00,900
Leave it to me.

102
00:06:00,900 --> 00:06:02,300
It's a piece of cake, dear.

103
00:06:02,800 --> 00:06:05,320
If you lose, you'll pay me back double!

104
00:06:06,300 --> 00:06:07,793
I'm fine. Well then,

105
00:06:07,843 --> 00:06:11,086
I need to get myself in shape for tomorrow.

106
00:06:11,136 --> 00:06:14,880
I'll take my leave for today.
Here we go, one, two, shoulder bar!

107
00:06:16,440 --> 00:06:18,741
He's unbearably full of himself, you know.

108
00:06:18,791 --> 00:06:20,600
Is he really going to be all right?

109
00:06:20,960 --> 00:06:24,393
Well, even in all of Japan,
few can match the senior officer's stamina,

110
00:06:24,443 --> 00:06:26,040
there aren't many of them, you know.

111
00:06:26,260 --> 00:06:28,060
Yes, that much is certain.

112
00:06:31,880 --> 00:06:33,940
Right, let's hit one more place!

113
00:06:35,840 --> 00:06:39,300
But senpai,
are you really okay for the sports day?

114
00:06:40,540 --> 00:06:44,400
The opponents are all lazy people
on the verge of lifestyle diseases.

115
00:06:44,820 --> 00:06:47,500
Do you think those guys would be a
match for me in the sumo loincloth?

116
00:06:48,960 --> 00:06:55,200
Yeah, you're right. Unless they bring in an Olympic athlete,
nobody's going to beat you, senpai.

117
00:06:55,200 --> 00:06:58,440
Exactly. Since that's settled,
let's go to the next place!

118
00:06:58,440 --> 00:06:58,980
Aaaaah!

119
00:07:01,720 --> 00:07:07,760
Today is a perfect day for a sports festival.
It is truly a joyful occasion.

120
00:07:08,480 --> 00:07:19,980
Now, our school's motto is to deepen the bond between parents and children.
For that reason, I hope the parents will take this opportunity to join in the events.

121
00:07:19,980 --> 00:07:22,040
I wonder what's keeping Ryo-chan? He's late.

122
00:07:22,540 --> 00:07:26,040
That idiot!
Late even on a day this important!

123
00:07:26,040 --> 00:07:27,820
Isn't that him?

124
00:07:28,120 --> 00:07:28,680
Yo.

125
00:07:28,680 --> 00:07:31,200
Yo.

126
00:07:31,200 --> 00:07:32,500
Honda-san.

127
00:07:32,900 --> 00:07:33,680
What happened?

128
00:07:34,160 --> 00:07:37,320
We've been drinking together
since last night, but

129
00:07:38,720 --> 00:07:39,600
What?

130
00:07:39,900 --> 00:07:45,880
I fell asleep partway through, but apparently the
senpai kept drinking until just a little while ago.

131
00:07:45,880 --> 00:07:48,360
My head, ow ow

132
00:07:48,360 --> 00:07:49,680
Mm...

133
00:07:51,740 --> 00:08:00,080
Good grief, are you all right in this state?
Hey, senior, please wake up, senior!

134
00:08:00,760 --> 00:08:07,420
Senior, you can't be so soft about it. Yeah.

135
00:08:08,840 --> 00:08:09,520
Ugh...

136
00:08:09,520 --> 00:08:10,680
I can't drink anymore.

137
00:08:10,680 --> 00:08:14,680
Hey, that's cold! What are you doing?

138
00:08:14,680 --> 00:08:16,180
Are you awake now, you idiot?

139
00:08:16,180 --> 00:08:17,300
Chief

140
00:08:17,300 --> 00:08:19,600
Senior, it's sports day!

141
00:08:19,600 --> 00:08:21,360
Sports day

142
00:08:21,360 --> 00:08:25,380
It's Daisuke's sports day!
It's about to start!

143
00:08:26,120 --> 00:08:28,160
Right, that's right.

144
00:08:28,160 --> 00:08:32,920
Pull yourself together, Ryotsu! The parents'
100-meter race is coming up right away!

145
00:08:32,920 --> 00:08:35,540
Senior, can you run?

146
00:08:35,540 --> 00:08:36,760
I'm fine.

147
00:08:48,740 --> 00:08:53,020
Hahaha, this is fine, no need to worry.
It's just the right handicap.

148
00:08:53,580 --> 00:08:56,680
The first event is the 100-meter
dash for the neighborhood.

149
00:08:57,040 --> 00:08:59,600
Participants,
please gather at the first gate.

150
00:09:00,640 --> 00:09:03,080
Alright, leave it to me.

151
00:09:10,700 --> 00:09:13,260
Are you really going to be okay, Ryo-chan?

152
00:09:13,260 --> 00:09:17,000
Easy, easy.
Let's see, I'm on the red team, right?

153
00:09:18,740 --> 00:09:20,100
Hey, that looks familiar.

154
00:09:20,660 --> 00:09:23,980
Isn't that J-League
player Tsuruta over there?

155
00:09:24,220 --> 00:09:24,820
What?

156
00:09:25,060 --> 00:09:27,960
Yes, it's Tsuruta, the national team player.

157
00:09:27,960 --> 00:09:29,740
Why is someone like that here?

158
00:09:30,180 --> 00:09:32,500
Don't be so quick to be surprised.
Look over there.

159
00:09:33,540 --> 00:09:35,780
It's Olympian Shunsuke Hayami!

160
00:09:36,200 --> 00:09:40,000
What? There's a Japanese
100m record holder here?

161
00:09:40,380 --> 00:09:43,920
Yes, he's a first-year's father.
This is a prestigious school, after all.

162
00:09:44,500 --> 00:09:46,820
Damn, an unexpected powerful rival...

163
00:09:48,740 --> 00:09:54,580
Isn't there? There is! See?
Phew, I'm saved. I can't handle this alone.

164
00:09:55,320 --> 00:10:03,080
There's the Japanese painter Nanyama Hakusai,
the composer Jean Valley, and a university professor, all going all out!

165
00:10:03,980 --> 00:10:09,720
We really have to get serious, or we're in trouble!
100m, the start is just about to begin!

166
00:10:12,220 --> 00:10:14,320
I hope we don't face a tough opponent.

167
00:10:14,920 --> 00:10:16,760
No sweat, not with Ryo-san.

168
00:10:19,440 --> 00:10:20,240
Get set...

169
00:10:21,960 --> 00:10:23,960
And the first heat is underway!

170
00:10:24,440 --> 00:10:26,480
Tsuruta has already shot out in front!

171
00:10:26,480 --> 00:10:29,220
He's left the other
runners behind in no time.

172
00:10:29,780 --> 00:10:31,860
Tsuruta's already into the final straight.

173
00:10:31,860 --> 00:10:32,940
Goal!

174
00:10:32,940 --> 00:10:35,440
As expected, first place goes to Tsuruta.

175
00:10:35,440 --> 00:10:36,800
What's the time?

176
00:10:37,320 --> 00:10:39,340
It's 10.09 seconds!

177
00:10:40,020 --> 00:10:43,960
A 10-second time in an
elementary school parents' race?!

178
00:10:43,960 --> 00:10:45,820
Now it's finally your turn, senpai.

179
00:10:45,820 --> 00:10:47,520
Ryo-san, do your best!

180
00:10:47,520 --> 00:10:52,160
And in this heat is Japanese
record holder Hayami.

181
00:10:52,160 --> 00:10:55,660
Can he beat Tsuruta's earlier time?

182
00:10:55,660 --> 00:10:56,660
On your marks.

183
00:10:58,620 --> 00:11:00,120
Same heat as him?!

184
00:11:00,840 --> 00:11:01,720
Get set...

185
00:11:03,580 --> 00:11:05,440
Ryo-san, do your best!

186
00:11:05,440 --> 00:11:07,440
Yes!

187
00:11:09,580 --> 00:11:11,600
Hayami got off to a light start,

188
00:11:11,600 --> 00:11:13,420
but in no time, he's at the top.

189
00:11:14,080 --> 00:11:14,680
Whoa!

190
00:11:14,680 --> 00:11:16,940
The crowd is really getting going!

191
00:11:16,940 --> 00:11:20,360
There's a runner tearing after
Hayami with tremendous momentum!

192
00:11:21,620 --> 00:11:22,360
Damn it!

193
00:11:22,360 --> 00:11:25,140
Some nobody has made it into the race and is catching up,
damn him!

194
00:11:27,160 --> 00:11:27,880
Whoa!

195
00:11:27,880 --> 00:11:29,260
Neck and neck again!

196
00:11:29,260 --> 00:11:32,480
No, an ordinary civilian
has caught up with Hayami!

197
00:11:33,480 --> 00:11:37,380
- So close
- That was a strong jet heat.

198
00:11:37,760 --> 00:11:39,510
Go!

199
00:11:39,560 --> 00:11:42,560
First place, Hayami!

200
00:11:42,880 --> 00:11:45,600
- Too bad.
- So close

201
00:11:45,900 --> 00:11:48,660
Idiot! You lack guts, Ryotsu!

202
00:11:51,400 --> 00:11:53,740
This is unbearable from the very start.

203
00:11:53,980 --> 00:11:57,800
W-what! An amazing record has been set!
It's a Japanese record!

204
00:11:58,000 --> 00:12:01,480
Hayami has broken his own Japanese record!

205
00:12:03,480 --> 00:12:06,500
Me too, me too! Aren't I a sick man too?

206
00:12:06,500 --> 00:12:08,300
Don't mess with me.

207
00:12:18,940 --> 00:12:20,620
On your marks

208
00:12:22,120 --> 00:12:23,240
Get set

209
00:12:25,880 --> 00:12:27,200
Okay, help me

210
00:12:27,740 --> 00:12:28,560
Help

211
00:12:39,480 --> 00:12:42,860
Good for him

212
00:12:42,860 --> 00:12:44,440
I wonder if he practiced hard.

213
00:12:44,440 --> 00:12:45,140
Yeah.

214
00:12:45,660 --> 00:12:48,680
Ryotsu,
why don't you take a lesson from Daisuke?

215
00:12:49,220 --> 00:12:52,120
Next is the hammer throw event.

216
00:12:54,440 --> 00:12:56,120
Alright, this time I've got it.

217
00:13:01,760 --> 00:13:04,600
So close!
It landed right on the 85-meter line.

218
00:13:04,600 --> 00:13:08,180
Mizoguchi of the white team
fell just one meter short.

219
00:13:08,180 --> 00:13:11,460
Isn't that Mizoguchi, the Olympian?

220
00:13:12,400 --> 00:13:16,720
Why are there so many
Olympic and pro athletes here?

221
00:13:17,540 --> 00:13:18,700
Is this even allowed?

222
00:13:30,940 --> 00:13:32,120
We're 28 points behind.

223
00:13:32,720 --> 00:13:35,280
Daisuke got first place, and now this!

224
00:13:35,280 --> 00:13:37,320
Ryotsu, do something about it.

225
00:13:39,060 --> 00:13:40,440
Easier said than done.

226
00:13:40,440 --> 00:13:43,380
No matter how hard we try,
the other team is just too strong.

227
00:13:43,380 --> 00:13:45,220
You've got to make it work somehow.

228
00:13:45,220 --> 00:13:47,240
I won't tolerate losing, Ryotsu.

229
00:13:47,240 --> 00:13:47,720
No way.

230
00:13:48,480 --> 00:13:50,780
Next up is the parents' tug-of-war.

231
00:13:50,780 --> 00:13:51,520
Good.

232
00:13:52,320 --> 00:13:54,940
Senpai, please do your best this time.

233
00:13:56,480 --> 00:13:58,680
Tug-of-war is my specialty.

234
00:13:58,680 --> 00:13:59,340
Well then.

235
00:13:59,340 --> 00:13:59,820
What?

236
00:14:00,280 --> 00:14:02,640
There are sumo wrestlers! Sumo wrestlers!

237
00:14:03,080 --> 00:14:03,920
The red team...

238
00:14:07,580 --> 00:14:09,400
So it's these guys after all.

239
00:14:10,060 --> 00:14:12,880
Listen,
the other team has two sumo wrestlers!

240
00:14:12,880 --> 00:14:14,820
We can't beat them in a fair fight.

241
00:14:14,820 --> 00:14:15,500
So,

242
00:14:15,860 --> 00:14:18,120
Now, the parents' tug-of-war!

243
00:14:18,120 --> 00:14:20,600
Which will win, red or white?

244
00:14:21,040 --> 00:14:23,920
The white team with the sumo wrestlers has the advantage,
after all?

245
00:14:24,360 --> 00:14:24,720
Here we go!

246
00:14:26,120 --> 00:14:27,780
Each of you, pull!

247
00:14:28,720 --> 00:14:30,780
Not good.

248
00:14:31,920 --> 00:14:32,480
7

249
00:14:34,640 --> 00:14:36,120
Each of you,

250
00:14:36,720 --> 00:14:37,580
Okay, now!

251
00:14:37,580 --> 00:14:40,100
Now!

252
00:14:40,640 --> 00:14:41,120
Red team!

253
00:14:41,120 --> 00:14:43,940
Looks like the red team's winning,
surprisingly.

254
00:14:43,940 --> 00:14:44,820
Here it comes.

255
00:14:44,820 --> 00:14:47,280
Yay, we're winning,
we're winning, we did it!

256
00:14:47,280 --> 00:14:47,880
We did it, we did it!

257
00:14:47,880 --> 00:14:49,040
That's a bit underhanded, isn't it?

258
00:14:49,040 --> 00:14:51,900
Ryo-san really is amazing, Mom!

259
00:14:52,740 --> 00:14:54,140
He's really reliable, isn't he.

260
00:14:59,960 --> 00:15:02,320
The afternoon session
will resume at 1 o'clock.

261
00:15:03,160 --> 00:15:06,380
Now, build up your stamina and
do your best this afternoon too.

262
00:15:06,840 --> 00:15:10,320
Alright, eat up, and we'll turn things
around all at once this afternoon.

263
00:15:11,100 --> 00:15:13,320
Don't eat so much that you can't run.

264
00:15:13,820 --> 00:15:15,520
I'm fine, this much is nothing.

265
00:15:15,520 --> 00:15:18,700
It'd be even better if I could
get a little buzz from some beer.

266
00:15:18,700 --> 00:15:22,880
You drank that much and
you can still drink more?

267
00:15:22,880 --> 00:15:26,060
For me, alcohol is just like gasoline,

268
00:15:26,060 --> 00:15:30,280
but for you, it's more like water, isn't it?

269
00:15:30,640 --> 00:15:34,280
Here's water, the real thing. Drink this.

270
00:15:34,280 --> 00:15:35,120
Eeeh!

271
00:15:36,840 --> 00:15:40,880
The first event of the afternoon
session is the parents' giant ball roll.

272
00:15:40,880 --> 00:15:41,920
Ready...

273
00:15:46,940 --> 00:15:49,740
Whoa, the red team is
moving incredibly fast!

274
00:15:49,740 --> 00:15:51,920
The white team is steadily pulling away.

275
00:15:58,020 --> 00:16:00,380
Goal! The red team wins!

276
00:16:03,640 --> 00:16:05,980
Next is the cavalry battle by K.

277
00:16:06,660 --> 00:16:07,060
Here we go!

278
00:16:08,900 --> 00:16:09,620
It's you!

279
00:16:10,020 --> 00:16:10,960
We won't lose!

280
00:16:11,120 --> 00:16:11,600
Coo!

281
00:16:14,200 --> 00:16:17,600
You can't take it!
It's glued on with instant adhesive!

282
00:16:17,800 --> 00:16:20,560
And on top of that, this one's Ninniko!

283
00:16:23,520 --> 00:16:24,320
Got it!

284
00:16:26,140 --> 00:16:27,020
Dosukoi!

285
00:16:28,220 --> 00:16:30,140
This is payback for before!

286
00:16:30,140 --> 00:16:31,660
Dosukoi!

287
00:16:31,660 --> 00:16:32,560
Damn it!

288
00:16:33,240 --> 00:16:33,860
Give it to me!

289
00:16:33,980 --> 00:16:34,420
Whoa!

290
00:16:34,640 --> 00:16:35,680
N-no way!

291
00:16:35,880 --> 00:16:37,160
A shrimp!

292
00:16:37,420 --> 00:16:38,100
Yes!

293
00:16:38,300 --> 00:16:39,800
He took out another one in one go!

294
00:16:40,040 --> 00:16:41,780
I mean, it's just like Ryo-chan,

295
00:16:41,780 --> 00:16:43,140
that's so like a senior officer, isn't it.

296
00:16:43,140 --> 00:16:45,240
As usual, he's a dirty bastard.

297
00:16:45,240 --> 00:16:48,140
Next is the parents' borrowed-item race!

298
00:16:52,840 --> 00:16:54,040
The National Diet Building!

299
00:16:54,820 --> 00:16:57,620
Collecting stamps from all around the Yamanote Line,
you mean?

300
00:16:57,620 --> 00:17:00,400
One traffic light? That's impossible.

301
00:17:00,400 --> 00:17:02,360
It's not impossible!

302
00:17:03,560 --> 00:17:04,820
I borrowed a car.

303
00:17:05,560 --> 00:17:05,920
No way.

304
00:17:06,700 --> 00:17:09,580
The red team is closing in,
now just 10 points behind the white team.

305
00:17:10,020 --> 00:17:10,920
Only two events left.

306
00:17:10,920 --> 00:17:15,620
If we win this 800m relay and the parent-child three-legged race,
we can turn it around.

307
00:17:15,620 --> 00:17:17,560
But when it comes to the senior relay,

308
00:17:17,560 --> 00:17:20,320
our opponents are Hayami and Tsuruta!

309
00:17:20,980 --> 00:17:22,500
Compared to that, over here

310
00:17:24,660 --> 00:17:26,300
Just as I thought, it's those guys.

311
00:17:26,300 --> 00:17:27,900
What do we do, senpai?

312
00:17:29,380 --> 00:17:31,920
Well, only two races are left.

313
00:17:31,920 --> 00:17:34,360
First up is the borrowed-items relay race.

314
00:17:34,780 --> 00:17:36,900
As expected, Tsuruta is up first.

315
00:17:36,900 --> 00:17:39,560
That means Hayami is the anchor, then.

316
00:17:40,320 --> 00:17:41,240
On your marks,

317
00:17:42,820 --> 00:17:44,440
Ryo-san, do your best!

318
00:17:44,440 --> 00:17:45,720
Ryotsu!

319
00:17:46,280 --> 00:17:46,860
Get set...

320
00:17:49,560 --> 00:17:50,780
They're off!

321
00:17:50,780 --> 00:17:53,000
Leading the way is White Team's Tsuruta.

322
00:17:54,040 --> 00:17:55,520
The Red Team's runners
are right behind them.

323
00:17:56,140 --> 00:17:57,720
Red Team moves into the lead.

324
00:17:57,720 --> 00:17:59,200
Red Team's anchor.

325
00:18:00,540 --> 00:18:01,680
Red Team leads.

326
00:18:01,680 --> 00:18:02,600
White Team is still right there.

327
00:18:02,600 --> 00:18:04,260
The second runner passes the baton first.

328
00:18:04,260 --> 00:18:07,000
But before long, they're overtaken.

329
00:18:07,000 --> 00:18:09,780
White Team's third runner takes the baton.

330
00:18:09,780 --> 00:18:12,100
Red Team finally makes the handoff too.

331
00:18:12,100 --> 00:18:13,500
I planned for this all along.

332
00:18:14,000 --> 00:18:14,400
Yes!

333
00:18:17,160 --> 00:18:17,900
Switch!

334
00:18:19,000 --> 00:18:20,540
White team, third runner!

335
00:18:20,540 --> 00:18:22,360
They're pulling away from red!

336
00:18:22,360 --> 00:18:23,580
Look, red!

337
00:18:24,180 --> 00:18:25,700
Don't run so slowly!

338
00:18:25,700 --> 00:18:28,920
The white team has passed
the baton to the fourth runner.

339
00:18:30,100 --> 00:18:31,980
The red team has finally passed the baton.

340
00:18:31,980 --> 00:18:34,580
The white team is clearly in the lead.

341
00:18:35,920 --> 00:18:37,600
The red team's fourth runner is fast!

342
00:18:38,100 --> 00:18:40,140
In no time, they've taken back the lead.

343
00:18:40,560 --> 00:18:42,120
and they're widening the gap.

344
00:18:42,120 --> 00:18:43,160
Wait, isn't that...

345
00:18:43,160 --> 00:18:44,900
that's like Ryo-chan, isn't it?

346
00:18:44,900 --> 00:18:47,660
Red and white teams, baton pass by touch!

347
00:18:47,660 --> 00:18:50,220
The fifth and sixth runners
each cover 200 meters,

348
00:18:50,540 --> 00:18:51,700
can they hold their ground?

349
00:18:51,780 --> 00:18:53,820
Come on, red team, only half a lap left!

350
00:18:53,980 --> 00:18:55,400
Whoops! He fell!

351
00:18:55,440 --> 00:18:55,800
What?

352
00:18:56,600 --> 00:18:59,300
In the meantime,
the white team has taken the lead!

353
00:19:02,000 --> 00:19:02,820
Cute.

354
00:19:03,860 --> 00:19:06,520
The white team has taken
the lead over the red team!

355
00:19:07,000 --> 00:19:09,080
It's the final sprint! Go all out!

356
00:19:09,900 --> 00:19:10,280
Yes! Here we go!

357
00:19:10,280 --> 00:19:12,560
The baton is passed to the
red team's anchor runner!

358
00:19:12,860 --> 00:19:13,280
Red team is off!

359
00:19:14,560 --> 00:19:16,380
The red team has passed the baton too!

360
00:19:17,980 --> 00:19:18,940
Nyaa!

361
00:19:20,540 --> 00:19:22,560
Red team's Hayami is speeding
ahead toward a decisive victory.

362
00:19:22,560 --> 00:19:25,400
Whoa, the red team is moving
at incredible speed too!

363
00:19:25,400 --> 00:19:26,520
Nakaryo-chan too?

364
00:19:27,580 --> 00:19:29,060
Spy, do your best!

365
00:19:29,760 --> 00:19:32,640
Amazing, the red team's Hayami
is neck and neck with the leader!

366
00:19:32,640 --> 00:19:33,960
Goal!

367
00:19:34,260 --> 00:19:37,980
Red team takes first place,
narrowly beating Hayami!

368
00:19:37,980 --> 00:19:40,500
Narrowly beating Hayami!

369
00:19:40,500 --> 00:19:41,460
Red team!

370
00:19:42,120 --> 00:19:45,320
With the red team's comeback,
the gap has finally shrunk to nine points!

371
00:19:46,600 --> 00:19:49,460
I'm tired. My throat is so dry.

372
00:19:57,700 --> 00:20:00,000
It hurts! Stop!

373
00:20:02,700 --> 00:20:11,060
Ryo-san!

374
00:20:11,380 --> 00:20:11,920
Ryotsu!

375
00:20:12,400 --> 00:20:13,580
Ryo-chan, are you okay?

376
00:20:15,540 --> 00:20:18,100
I'm fine. The last one is the
two-person three-legged race.

377
00:20:18,100 --> 00:20:19,100
Ryo-san, you can't do this.

378
00:20:19,100 --> 00:20:20,600
It's nothing. This much is nothing.

379
00:20:20,600 --> 00:20:25,440
Ryo-san, don't push yourself.
You've already done so well.

380
00:20:25,440 --> 00:20:28,380
And now, the final event: the
parent-child two-person three-legged race!

381
00:20:28,380 --> 00:20:30,800
Participants,
please gather at Entrance Gate A.

382
00:20:30,800 --> 00:20:32,760
Right, the final race

383
00:20:33,400 --> 00:20:34,460
I'll run.

384
00:20:34,820 --> 00:20:37,080
What about your leg?

385
00:20:37,080 --> 00:20:41,440
It's not perfect,
but I'll do my best for Daisuke somehow.

386
00:20:42,880 --> 00:20:43,460
Papa

387
00:20:44,200 --> 00:20:45,100
Listen, Daisuke.

388
00:20:45,460 --> 00:20:47,580
In a three-legged race, you don't run alone.

389
00:20:47,580 --> 00:20:49,540
You've got to help me carry my share.

390
00:20:49,540 --> 00:20:50,160
Okay.

391
00:20:50,900 --> 00:20:51,260
Good.

392
00:20:51,760 --> 00:20:53,800
You two, do your best!

393
00:20:53,800 --> 00:20:54,540
I love you.

394
00:20:54,540 --> 00:20:55,540
Good luck.

395
00:20:55,540 --> 00:20:56,140
Yeah.

396
00:20:56,800 --> 00:20:58,520
Ryo-san, I'll do my best!

397
00:21:00,200 --> 00:21:01,540
Good, that's the spirit!

398
00:21:02,260 --> 00:21:02,980
On your marks...

399
00:21:04,620 --> 00:21:06,120
And now, the final race!

400
00:21:06,120 --> 00:21:08,540
It's the start of the
parent-child three-legged race!

401
00:21:08,540 --> 00:21:09,860
I love you, do your best!

402
00:21:09,860 --> 00:21:10,640
Honey!

403
00:21:10,640 --> 00:21:11,680
I love you!

404
00:21:12,820 --> 00:21:16,213
1, 2, 1, 2, 1, 2, 1, 2, 1, 2, 1, 2, 1,

405
00:21:16,263 --> 00:21:19,971
2, 1, 2, 1, 2, 1, 2, 1, 2, 1, 2, 1, 2, 1,

406
00:21:20,021 --> 00:21:23,705
2, 1, 2, 1, 2, 1, 2, 1, 2, 1, 2, 1, 2, 1,

407
00:21:23,755 --> 00:21:27,489
2, 1, 2, 1, 2, 1, 2, 1, 2, 1, 2, 1, 2, 1,

408
00:21:27,539 --> 00:21:31,211
2, 1, 2, 1, 2, 1, 2, 1, 2, 1, 2, 1, 2, 1,

409
00:21:31,261 --> 00:21:34,982
2, 1, 2, 1, 2, 1, 2, 1, 2, 1, 2, 1, 2, 1,

410
00:21:35,032 --> 00:21:38,729
2, 1, 2, 1, 2, 1, 2, 1, 2, 1, 2, 1, 2, 1,

411
00:21:38,779 --> 00:21:42,660
2, 1, 2, 1, 2, 1, 2, 1, 2, 1, 2, 1, 2, 1, 2

412
00:21:43,380 --> 00:21:46,680
The red team suddenly slows down!

413
00:21:46,680 --> 00:21:48,340
They're being passed one after another.

414
00:21:49,580 --> 00:21:51,380
Daisuke, don't give up!

415
00:21:51,380 --> 00:21:53,240
That's right, we're going to turn it around!

416
00:21:53,840 --> 00:21:55,620
The white team's first
runner takes first place.

417
00:21:55,620 --> 00:21:57,980
Next, the white team's second
runner also crosses the finish line.

418
00:21:57,980 --> 00:22:01,100
A little behind, the red team's second
runner has also crossed the finish line.

419
00:22:02,160 --> 00:22:05,980
The red team's first runner, who had some
trouble along the way, is also running desperately.

420
00:22:05,980 --> 00:22:08,660
Dad, don't push yourself anymore.
Let's just stop.

421
00:22:09,300 --> 00:22:12,500
Daisuke, don't give up!
The finish line is just a little further.

422
00:22:12,680 --> 00:22:14,860
Let's run to the end together,
with both of our strength.

423
00:22:14,860 --> 00:22:16,360
Yeah, got it.

424
00:22:16,360 --> 00:22:18,520
Daisuke, just a little more!

425
00:22:18,520 --> 00:22:20,160
Keep going, last stretch!

426
00:22:20,160 --> 00:22:22,180
Dear, Daisuke!

427
00:22:23,120 --> 00:22:25,380
Come on,
the red team's anchor didn't give up either,

428
00:22:25,380 --> 00:22:27,040
and finally crossed the finish line.

429
00:22:27,780 --> 00:22:29,080
You did great, Daisuke!

430
00:22:29,080 --> 00:22:31,460
You didn't give up and
ran all the way to the end.

431
00:22:31,460 --> 00:22:33,840
Yeah, Daddy worked hard too.

432
00:22:34,340 --> 00:22:34,900
You.

433
00:22:38,540 --> 00:22:40,400
Honey, Daisuke.

434
00:22:40,400 --> 00:22:41,620
That was wonderful.

435
00:22:42,640 --> 00:22:45,560
Even an ogre sheds tears!

436
00:22:45,860 --> 00:22:48,660
Hey, what are you doing
to an injured person?!

437
00:22:49,020 --> 00:22:52,100
Same injured person,
but what a difference from Hideo!

438
00:22:52,280 --> 00:22:53,620
Aw, come on!

439
00:23:01,260 --> 00:23:03,240
We lost in the end!

440
00:23:03,460 --> 00:23:07,160
But that's fine, isn't it!
Daisuke got some good memories out of it!

441
00:23:07,360 --> 00:23:09,840
That's right!
It's not about winning or losing!

442
00:23:09,840 --> 00:23:13,700
It is about winning or losing. You still have to pay back the ten thousand yen,
don't you?

443
00:23:13,880 --> 00:23:14,540
Ryotsu!

444
00:23:14,540 --> 00:23:16,199
G-gah, C-Chief.

445
00:23:16,249 --> 00:23:18,600
About the ten thousand yen, well...

446
00:23:19,200 --> 00:23:22,380
I don't mind about that.
In exchange, I have a favor to ask.

447
00:23:24,680 --> 00:23:27,174
Take part in my younger
sister Sakura's sports day.

448
00:23:27,224 --> 00:23:29,260
This time, you're going to win it all.

449
00:23:31,220 --> 00:23:32,957
100 and 1, 100 and 2,

450
00:23:33,007 --> 00:23:35,540
100 and 3, 100 and 4, 100 and...

451
00:23:39,000 --> 00:23:42,660
Since it's affiliated with an international kindergarten,
it's an international competition!

452
00:23:42,660 --> 00:23:44,620
There are even world record holders here!

453
00:23:45,080 --> 00:23:46,580
That's allowed?!

454
00:23:49,640 --> 00:23:51,740
What? The Chief's at a wedding?

455
00:23:51,740 --> 00:23:53,140
Nakagawa's in Europe.

456
00:23:53,140 --> 00:23:54,740
And Terai's supposedly sick too.

457
00:23:54,740 --> 00:23:56,820
So it's just you and Reiko today

458
00:23:57,560 --> 00:23:59,760
Maria, what are you doing all of a sudden?

459
00:23:59,760 --> 00:24:01,960
Just because it's only me and Reiko...

460
00:24:01,960 --> 00:24:04,160
Nothing's going to happen, you know!

461
00:24:05,540 --> 00:24:07,740
This two-person police box,
take good care of it!

462
00:24:08,600 --> 00:24:10,780
That's Kameari.

463
00:24:11,600 --> 00:24:14,140
Kameari Park Police Box!

464
00:24:15,260 --> 00:24:19,140
Everyone, come on over to our town!

465
00:24:20,220 --> 00:24:20,740
Thank you!

